{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact be90ff0527119800ded273cb8180e548a0710407 on request/scope-contract-r15, under promise git:sha1…57165ef on request git:sha1…f2c7bab\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 18 at be90ff0527119800ded273cb8180e548a0710407, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict 8645c22b on 5a15b9b0. All four subjects; the two companions are unchanged. Finding 1, the item type as one path component: one reversible rule replaces three that disagreed. To write: an ASCII letter, a digit, hyphen, underscore or dot is written as itself; every other byte of the name's UTF-8 is a percent sign and two upper-case hex digits, with no exception for colon, at-sign, slash, percent, space or tilde; a name that is exactly one dot is written tilde dot, and two dots tilde dot dot, so a tilde appears only in those two components. To read: split the path at slashes first, then read the component by the rule. Normal form decodes only a byte the rule writes as itself. The dot names are not written with an encoded dot, because the URL standard that browsers and the serving platform follow removes encoded dot segments; that is the author's knowledge of the standard and no parser was run, so a source row owes a check with the platform's own parser. Witness 18.42 grows from 14 to 40 cases, with ten hostile names round-tripped; the paper pass found and fixed one collision in the first draft. Finding 2, item links: a fourth relation is named, the same selector, for two item URIs with equal scope ID, type and position where at least one states no incarnation; they may name different items and are never called the same reference. The same reference for items needs both incarnations stated and equal, or both resolved with answers that state the same incarnation and the same opening fact; the answer to an item URI now states both. The two-hosts, one-seed, two-incarnations case is recorded. Non-blocking points applied: a fact reference built from a URI takes its kind from the seed or the verified entry; the sentence that made a numeric own position a rule's fault is withdrawn and a source row owes the check; three source rows carry the commission's outputs (canonical URIs in notes, logs, replay and client output; the scope URI in a label's answer; the duties for copying or forwarding between installations, listed as not designed, with its owner). Source rows: 30. One limit is stated: a server between the reader and the route that decodes an encoded slash would break the path of a name that contains a slash; it cannot yield a false proof, because an item URI proves nothing. Reading limits: single writer; one range of effects.ts was read. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"be90ff0527119800ded273cb8180e548a0710407","path":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md"}}